---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import GRCAlert from '../components/GRCAlert.astro';
---

<BaseLayout 
  title="Regulatory Framework Guides"
  description="Authoritative reference guides and executive cheat-sheets for the EU AI Act, NIST AI RMF, ISO/IEC 42001, and SOC 2."
>
  <div class="max-w-7xl mx-auto px-4 sm:px-6 lg:px-8 py-12 lg:py-20">
    
    <div class="max-w-3xl mb-16">
      <span class="text-xs font-mono font-bold tracking-widest uppercase text-blue-700">Knowledge Base</span>
      <h1 class="text-3xl sm:text-5xl font-extrabold text-[#0A2540] tracking-tight mt-2 leading-tight">
        Core Compliance & AI Frameworks
      </h1>
      <p class="mt-4 text-base sm:text-lg text-slate-600 leading-relaxed font-normal">
        A structured breakdown of the dominant regulatory instruments shaping enterprise AI, data privacy, and information security.
      </p>
    </div>

    <!-- Framework 1: EU AI Act -->
    <section id="eu-ai-act" class="mb-16 p-8 sm:p-10 rounded-xl bg-white border border-slate-200 shadow-corporate scroll-mt-24">
      <div class="flex flex-wrap items-center justify-between gap-4 mb-4">
        <span class="px-2.5 py-0.5 rounded text-xs font-bold uppercase tracking-wider bg-blue-50 text-blue-800 border border-blue-200">
          European Union Regulation
        </span>
        <span class="text-xs font-mono text-slate-500">Enforcement 2024–2026+</span>
      </div>
      <h2 class="text-2xl sm:text-3xl font-bold text-[#0A2540] tracking-tight">
        The EU Artificial Intelligence Act (EU AI Act)
      </h2>
      <p class="mt-3 text-slate-600 text-sm sm:text-base leading-relaxed max-w-3xl font-normal">
        The world's first comprehensive horizontal legal framework for artificial intelligence. Operates on a risk-based classification model, imposing proportional requirements based on potential harm.
      </p>

      <div class="grid grid-cols-1 sm:grid-cols-2 lg:grid-cols-4 gap-4 mt-8">
        <div class="p-4 rounded-lg bg-red-50 border border-red-200">
          <span class="text-xs font-bold font-mono text-red-800 block mb-1">PROHIBITED</span>
          <p class="text-xs text-slate-700">Social scoring, cognitive manipulation, biometric categorization of protected traits.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="p-4 rounded-lg bg-amber-50 border border-amber-200">
          <span class="text-xs font-bold font-mono text-amber-800 block mb-1">HIGH-RISK (Annex III)</span>
          <p class="text-xs text-slate-700">Employment recruitment, critical infrastructure, credit scoring, law enforcement.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="p-4 rounded-lg bg-blue-50 border border-blue-200">
          <span class="text-xs font-bold font-mono text-blue-800 block mb-1">TRANSPARENCY</span>
          <p class="text-xs text-slate-700">Generative AI, deepfakes, conversational chatbots interacting with consumers.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="p-4 rounded-lg bg-emerald-50 border border-emerald-200">
          <span class="text-xs font-bold font-mono text-emerald-800 block mb-1">MINIMAL RISK</span>
          <p class="text-xs text-slate-700">AI video games, spam filters, predictive maintenance (free of obligations).</p>
        </div>
      </div>

      <GRCAlert type="alert" title="Statutory Enforcement Timeline">
        Prohibited AI systems take effect first (6 months post-entry into force), followed by General Purpose AI (GPAI) governance (12 months), and High-Risk compliance (24–36 months).
      </GRCAlert>
    </section>

    <!-- Framework 2: NIST AI RMF -->
    <section id="nist-ai-rmf" class="mb-16 p-8 sm:p-10 rounded-xl bg-white border border-slate-200 shadow-corporate scroll-mt-24">
      <div class="flex flex-wrap items-center justify-between gap-4 mb-4">
        <span class="px-2.5 py-0.5 rounded text-xs font-bold uppercase tracking-wider bg-blue-50 text-blue-800 border border-blue-200">
          U.S. National Standard
        </span>
        <span class="text-xs font-mono text-slate-500">NIST AI 100-1</span>
      </div>
      <h2 class="text-2xl sm:text-3xl font-bold text-[#0A2540] tracking-tight">
        NIST AI Risk Management Framework (AI RMF 1.0)
      </h2>
      <p class="mt-3 text-slate-600 text-sm sm:text-base leading-relaxed max-w-3xl font-normal">
        A voluntary, flexible, and non-prescriptive framework developed to assist organizations in designing, developing, and deploying trustworthy AI systems.
      </p>

      <div class="grid grid-cols-1 sm:grid-cols-2 lg:grid-cols-4 gap-4 mt-8">
        <div class="p-4 rounded-lg bg-slate-50 border border-slate-200">
          <h3 class="text-sm font-bold text-slate-900 mb-1">1. GOVERN</h3>
          <p class="text-xs text-slate-600">Culture, risk management accountability, organizational policies, and legal oversight.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="p-4 rounded-lg bg-slate-50 border border-slate-200">
          <h3 class="text-sm font-bold text-slate-900 mb-1">2. MAP</h3>
          <p class="text-xs text-slate-600">Context categorization, understanding positive/negative impacts, third-party dependencies.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="p-4 rounded-lg bg-slate-50 border border-slate-200">
          <h3 class="text-sm font-bold text-slate-900 mb-1">3. MEASURE</h3>
          <p class="text-xs text-slate-600">Quantitative and qualitative metrics: model accuracy, bias audits, robustness, red-teaming.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="p-4 rounded-lg bg-slate-50 border border-slate-200">
          <h3 class="text-sm font-bold text-slate-900 mb-1">4. MANAGE</h3>
          <p class="text-xs text-slate-600">Prioritizing risks, allocating treatment resources, feedback loops, and incident de-escalation.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- Framework 3: ISO/IEC 42001 -->
    <section id="iso-42001" class="mb-16 p-8 sm:p-10 rounded-xl bg-white border border-slate-200 shadow-corporate scroll-mt-24">
      <div class="flex flex-wrap items-center justify-between gap-4 mb-4">
        <span class="px-2.5 py-0.5 rounded text-xs font-bold uppercase tracking-wider bg-blue-50 text-blue-800 border border-blue-200">
          International Certifiable Standard
        </span>
        <span class="text-xs font-mono text-slate-500">Published Dec 2023</span>
      </div>
      <h2 class="text-2xl sm:text-3xl font-bold text-[#0A2540] tracking-tight">
        ISO/IEC 42001:2023 (AI Management System)
      </h2>
      <p class="mt-3 text-slate-600 text-sm sm:text-base leading-relaxed max-w-3xl font-normal">
        The international gold standard for organizations providing or utilizing AI-based products or services. Modeled after ISO 27001 (ISMS) using the Harmonized High-Level Structure.
      </p>

      <GRCAlert type="action" title="Integration with ISO 27001">
        Organizations already certified in ISO 27001 can integrate ISO 42001 directly into their existing management system (AIMS), sharing common clauses like leadership commitment, internal audits, and management reviews.
      </GRCAlert>
    </section>

  </div>
</BaseLayout>